in @prism

in @optics
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens
in @mirror/lens/cli

# @mirror/lens/cli/crack — kintsugi geometry as a stage.
#
# Eighth of eight verb sub-stages forward-promised in
# docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3 (table at §3 + §3.1 shape sketch).
# Closes the §3 forward-promise: with this shard landing, all eight
# sub-stages of @mirror/lens/cli are minted and the CLI directory IS
# self-describing by `ls` per §3.
#
# === The third-state lifecycle, condensed ===
#
# Per cli-as-prism §2.1 + §5.1 (THE sharpest condensation): the
# cybernetic CLI's third-state lifecycle had FOUR verbs — `cracks`,
# `open`, `force`, `seal`. The recursive condensation collapsed all
# four into ONE STAGE (crack) with the standard five operations,
# where the three settle modes (open / force / seal) are carried by
# a TYPED ENUM at the settle action's argument shape.
#
# Per Alex's call this tick: ONE action with typed enum, NOT three
# actions. The cybernetic-cli's `mirror seal X` / `mirror crack open X`
# / `mirror crack force X` are user-surface affordances; the substrate
# signature is `crack_settle(target, mode: crack_mode)`. The CLI
# parser maps `--open` / `--force` / bare to the three enum variants.
#
# === The rename: hole → crack ===
#
# Per cli-as-prism §2.1 + §4.2: `\` produces fracture per
# `gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md` (the gap fold). With the `hole`
# framing, settle-with-flag felt arbitrary ("hole settle --open" reads
# as bookkeeping). With the `crack` framing, the kintsugi geometry
# makes the verb-with-typed-enum LITERAL: settling on a crack IS the
# gold pour. `mode_open` declares a new fracture (`\` event);
# `mode_force` accepts loss and forces the fill (`\!` event);
# `mode_seal` is the default (promote a converged `\` to explicit;
# gold pour). The lifecycle isn't being hidden under flags — the
# enum variants NAME the kintsugi acts.
#
# === crack_mode — inline declaration (forward-promise factor-out) ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] + [[feedback-no-stringly-types]]:
# the three crack settle modes are carried at substrate altitude as a
# typed sum, NOT as a `str` flag dispatcher. The substrate did not
# yet carry a `crack_mode` type as of this tick (verified by
# search across shards/); declaring it inline here per the precedent
# in observation.mirror's `unit_interval` and transparency.mirror's
# `dim_index` (substrate-pull tick I/II). Forward-promise to factor
# this type out to a substrate home (likely
# `shards/kintsugi/crack_mode.mirror`) when the kintsugi family root
# grows enough sub-shards to earn it; the kintsugi geometry is the
# crack_mode's natural family, not the CLI altitude.
#
# Variant semantics:
#   mode_open   declare a new fracture; `\` event; the user is
#               naming a gap-fold-substrate `\` site that wasn't
#               yet explicit. Substrate writes a new crack ref.
#   mode_force  accept loss + force fill; `\!` event per
#               [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] / kintsugi
#               variety-maintenance; honest about regression. The
#               substrate writes the fill AND the
#               transparency-tagged residual opacity (the loss is
#               named, not hidden).
#   mode_seal   default; promote a converged `\` to explicit; gold
#               pour. The kintsugi loop converged at this crack;
#               the settle records the closure and emits the proof.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Parent bench: @mirror/lens/cli (shards/mirror/lens/cli.mirror).
# Family root:  @mirror/lens    (shards/mirror/lens.mirror).
# Sibling stages:
#   @mirror/lens/cli/compile    — landed at 737330f
#   @mirror/lens/cli/kintsugi   — landed at ce2ef9b
#   @mirror/lens/cli/shatter    — landed at 9bc68f8
#   @mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap  — landed at ea9c9a7
#   @mirror/lens/cli/sh         — landed previously this tick
#   @mirror/lens/cli/reflect    — landed previously this tick
#   @mirror/lens/cli/time       — landed previously this tick
#
# After this shard lands: all 8 sub-stages of @mirror/lens/cli are
# minted; the CLI directory IS self-describing by `ls`
# (cli-as-prism §3 forward-promise CLOSED).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/lens/cli/crack.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/lens/cli/crack` and only that (plus the inline
# `crack_mode` type, forward-promised to factor out).
#
# === Note: no mirror.spec command yet ===
#
# Unlike compile / kintsugi / shatter, crack does NOT yet have a
# `command crack { ... }` declaration in mirror.spec — the
# kintsugi geometry surface is consumed by the runtime's crack
# walker directly rather than the mosaic build dispatch. This stage
# shard is the CLI surface forward-promised by cli-as-prism.md §3;
# the mirror.spec-side declaration is a subsequent Taut tick
# (forward-promise: when `mirror.spec` gains a `command crack
# { ... }` block, its arg shape carries the target ref + crack_mode
# enum this stage's actions already declare).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3, §3.1 (shape sketch),
#               §2.1 (crack row: open/force/seal collapse to settle +
#               typed enum),
#               §4.2 (the verb-with-typed-enum strain + kintsugi
#               geometry resolution),
#               §5.1 (THE sharpest condensation — 4 verbs → 1
#               sub-stage × 1 small enum),
#               §7 (default-op rule: crack declares `default focus`
#               — listing cracks is free; the settle path is the
#               gold pour, a real substrate write),
#               docs/specs/the-convergence.md §2 (the four-lens
#               table rows for crack open/force/seal),
#               docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.2 (stage),
#               gap-tension-tensor-substrate.md (the `\` event and
#               kintsugi geometry this stage carries).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (kintsugi
#                      bias = lift @facet -> @mirror; the gold pour
#                      IS the bias-aligned write),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (the
#                      variety-maintenance contract; force fill
#                      records the residual variety loss),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                      (the settle's proof block discharges via
#                      splinter(ast) per the property/fracture
#                      bilateral pattern),
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
#                      (stage IS a sub-prism specialization),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]
#                      (file path matches namespace),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (crack_mode is a
#                      typed enum, not a str flag),
#                      [[feedback-no-stringly-types]] (the three
#                      modes are substrate-altitude variants).
# Related shards: lens/cli.mirror (parent bench),
#                 lens/cli/kintsugi.mirror (sibling — kintsugi's
#                 tournament settles working-set fractures; crack's
#                 settle pours gold on individual cracks; the two
#                 stages share the kintsugi-engine altitude below),
#                 glass.mirror (imperfect / transparency carriers —
#                 transparency tags the residual opacity from
#                 mode_force fills).

# === crack_mode — typed sum at substrate altitude ===
#
# Inline declaration; forward-promise to factor out to
# `shards/kintsugi/crack_mode.mirror` when the kintsugi family root
# grows enough sub-shards to earn it. Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] / [[feedback-no-stringly-types]]: the
# three modes are substrate-altitude variants, not str flag values.
# Per Alex's call this tick: ONE settle action with typed enum, NOT
# three actions.
type crack_mode =
  | mode_open
  | mode_force
  | mode_seal

stage @mirror/lens/cli/crack {
  # Per cli-as-prism §7: crack declares `default focus` — listing
  # cracks is free. Bare `mirror crack` enumerates every open `\`
  # (the cybernetic-cli's `cracks` verb collapsed into focus). The
  # settle path is the gold pour — a real substrate write (the
  # kintsugi geometry's bias-aligned closure); the user pays only for
  # the explicit settle. The other read-shaped ops (project / split /
  # shift) walk the fracture set without writing.
  default focus

  # The five operations the produced prism exposes on the crack
  # sub-manifold (the fracture set; the union of open `\` sites the
  # kintsugi loop is tracking). Each operand below names the natural
  # shape of the manifold's element at that op's slot, per the spec
  # §3.1 sketch convention and §2.1's per-verb decisions:
  #   focus    target     — list every open `\` (the cybernetic-cli's
  #                          `cracks` verb)
  #   project  predicate  — filter the fracture set by predicate
  #                          (e.g. all cracks below a transparency
  #                          band; orthogonal projection per
  #                          [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]])
  #   split    candidate  — enumerate candidate fills for a crack
  #                          (graph-walk on the gap-tension manifold;
  #                          composes with kintsugi.split at the
  #                          tournament altitude)
  #   shift    basis      — view the same fracture set at a
  #                          different basis (e.g. eigenvalue-sorted
  #                          vs source-line-sorted; same content,
  #                          different declared frame;
  #                          [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]])
  #   settle   target     — the ONE write; pour gold along the
  #                          fracture; mode (open / force / seal)
  #                          carried by the typed crack_mode enum at
  #                          the action signature; emits proof block
  #                          recording the kintsugi act
  focus    target
  project  predicate
  split    candidate
  shift    basis
  settle   target
}

# === Crack-specific actions ===
#
# No mirror.spec `command crack { ... }` declaration yet (see the
# "no mirror.spec command yet" note above). The CLI surface action
# signature lands here as the substrate forward-promise; the Rust
# runtime walks this declaration when the kintsugi geometry surface
# lifts into the mosaic dispatch. Substrate-pull discipline per
# [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]].
#
# Honest `partials` from birth (per recognition #306): the return
# type is the substrate's `imperfect` functor (declared in
# shards/glass.mirror as `imperfect(a, e, l) = success(a) |
# partial(a, l) | failure(e, l)`).
#
# Per mode:
#   mode_open settle: success carries the declared crack ref;
#                     partial is rare (declaring a new fracture is
#                     usually clean); failure on duplicate-crack-at-
#                     site / write refusal.
#   mode_force settle: SUCCESS IS RARE BY CONSTRUCTION — the force
#                     path is explicitly accept-loss; the substrate
#                     ALMOST ALWAYS returns partial-with-loss
#                     carrying the transparency-tagged residual
#                     opacity (the `\!` event names the loss; the
#                     return shape carries it). Failure only on hard
#                     write error.
#   mode_seal settle: success carries the converged crack ref;
#                     partial-with-loss on tolerable convergence
#                     shortfall (the kintsugi loop got close but
#                     not all the way; the residual opacity is
#                     preserved for the next round); failure on
#                     hard read error (crack not in set, write
#                     refused).
#
# Per [[feedback-manual-closure-is-training-pull]]: dark regions are
# kintsugi's mutation targets, not manual patches; the
# partial-with-loss shape preserves them rather than hiding them
# under opaque carriers. The mode_force path is the substrate-aligned
# way to take honest regressions.

# crack() — enumerate every open `\` in the current fracture set
# (the default-focus behaviour). Returns the imperfect carrying the
# fracture-set ref on success; partial-with-loss on tolerable read
# shortfall; failure on hard read error.
crack() -> imperfect { \ }

# crack_settle(target, mode) — the ONE settle path; the typed
# crack_mode enum at the second arg position selects the kintsugi
# act (open / force / seal). Per Alex's call: ONE action with typed
# enum, NOT three actions. Returns the imperfect carrying the
# kintsugi-act result on success; partial-with-loss on tolerable
# variety-shortfall (rare for mode_open, EXPECTED for mode_force,
# possible for mode_seal); failure on hard write error.
crack_settle(target: ref, mode: crack_mode) -> imperfect { \ }

out @mirror/lens/cli/crack
out crack_mode
out mode_open
out mode_force
out mode_seal
out crack
out crack_settle
